SSR and browser suites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":75202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":160},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a1cc852-b0c1-49be-9302-8d1ff898434e","uuid":"6307779e-a6e9-435e-98c6-4443f537b011","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:55:44.978Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MAtTYupLZYJdkKyTMm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PKNfU2wdtmKy8MWFJ2w5Nx":{"command":"mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Ticket 02: server/browser attribute parity\n\nImplemented:\n- src/htm.ts: `_val` now unwraps `_Escaped` to its raw string, so plain\n  element attributes and host non-prop attributes are escaped once.\n  Host non-prop attrs follow browser rules: true -> '' (empty attr via\n  `_renderHost`), false/null/undefined omitted, else String(v).\n- src/builders.ts unchanged: `_renderHost` already renders '' as a bare\n  attribute.\n- test/parity.ts: shared table (plain + host attrs with & \" ' <, the four\n  boolean/null values, numbers, declared prop, nested markup, host\n  children). `stripMarkers` removes `<!--[-->`/`<!--]-->` only; ticket\n  for the `<!--[c-->` children marker must extend the regex.\n- test/ssr.ts runs it against server `html`; test/index.ts runs it\n  against browser `bhtml` and compares server vs browser.\n- AGENTS.md: note on the parity table.\n\nTDD: SSR test red (12 failures, double escaping and \"true\"/\"false\"\nstrings on hosts), then green. Browser test written after the fix;\nverified red (12 failures) by reverting src/htm.ts, then green.\n\nGotcha: htm requires `<input />`; `<input ...>` yields \"input[object Object]\".\nFresh worktree needs `npm run build` before `npm test` (typecheck uses dist).\nDelete example-hydration/build before lint.\n\nResults: npm run test:ssr 98/98, npm test 324/324, lint clean.\nEOF\ngit add src/htm.ts test/parity.ts test/ssr.ts test/index.ts AGENTS.md && git commit -qm \"Server and browser emit the same attributes\n\nUnwrap the templater's escaped wrapper in server attribute holes so\nvalues are escaped once, and apply the browser's true/false/null rules\nto non-prop host attributes. Add a shared parity table run by both the\nSSR and browser suites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short"}}}
