{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3MBhyZAht7BMbNpjXZN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Server output for an interpolated attribute holding `&`, `\"` or `<` contains the value escaped exactly once\n[x] A non-prop attribute on a component with value `true` renders as an empty attribute, and `false`, `null` and `undefined` render no attribute\n[x] Every parity table case produces equal HTML from the server templater and the browser `String()` path, markers aside\n[x] Existing exact-string static page assertions in the SSR suite pass unchanged\n[x] `npm run test:ssr` and `npm test` pass\n\nThe server templater now escapes interpolated attributes once and handles `true`, `false`, `null` and `undefined` the same way the browser does. It's committed as `7c00a68`. `npm run test:ssr` passes 98/98, `npm test` passes 324/324, and lint is clean.\n\n**The fix** is in `src/htm.ts`:\n- **Double escaping:** attribute values were being escaped twice. `_val` now unwraps the templater's escaped wrapper back to the original string before escaping, so plain-element attributes and host attributes get escaped once. A link like `/s?a=1&b=2` now comes out as `a=1&amp;b=2`, not `&amp;amp;`.\n- **Booleans and null on hosts:** for attributes passed to a component that aren't declared props, `true` becomes an empty attribute and `false`/`null`/`undefined` are left out. Before, they were written as the strings `\"true\"`, `\"false\"` and so on. `src/builders.ts` needed no change, since it already writes an empty value as a bare attribute.\n\n**The shared table** is `test/parity.ts`. Its 19 cases cover `&`, quotes and `<` in plain and host attributes, the four boolean/null values, numbers, a declared prop, nested markup and host children. `test/ssr.ts` runs it against the server output, and `test/index.ts` runs it against the browser `String()` output and also checks server equals browser. The existing exact-string SSR assertions are unchanged and still pass.\n\n**Order of work:** the SSR test failed first (12 failures), then passed after the fix. I wrote the browser test after the fix. To check it really catches the bug, I ran it against the old `src/htm.ts`: 12 failures, then green with the fix back in place.\n\n**For the later children-marker ticket:** `stripMarkers` only removes the current `<!--[-->` and `<!--]-->` markers. When `<!--[c-->` lands, its regex needs extending.\n\nI added a short note to `AGENTS.md` about the parity table. It also records that htm needs void tags written as `<input />`; `<input ...>` silently produces broken output. The details are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":75362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a1cc852-b0c1-49be-9302-8d1ff898434e","uuid":"4b4b9d53-b149-4aab-8cfc-f0b24d065170","timestamp":"2026-10-15T03:55:54.382Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3MBhhw98zrxbsQqhhRr"}
